us type=message.part.updated publishing\nINFO  2026-10-18T01:18:52 +0ms service=bus type=storage.write publishing\nINFO  2026-10-18T01:18:52 +0ms service=bus type=message.updated publishing\nINFO  2026-10-18T01:18:52 +0ms service=session session=ses_eb36948feffexs133iTzusEXWm type=finish part\nINFO  2026-10-18T01:18:52 +0ms service=bus type=storage.write publishing\nINFO  2026-10-18T01:18:52 +0ms service=bus type=message.updated publishing\nINFO  2026-10-18T01:18:52 +3ms service=bus type=storage.write publishing\nINFO  2026-10-18T01:18:52 +0ms service=bus type=message.updated publishing\nINFO  2026-10-18T01:18:52 +0ms service=session session=ses_eb36948feffexs133iTzusEXWm sessionID=ses_eb36948feffexs133iTzusEXWm unlocking\nINFO  2026-10-18T01:18:52 +0ms service=bus type=session.idle publishing\nI fixed six bugs in `catalog/`, but I couldn't run `python3 -m unittest` because I don't have a shell tool here. Please run it to confirm everything passes. I checked each fix against what its test expects.\n\n- `fees.py`: the fee was the number of days *plus* the daily rate; it's now days *times* the rate, so 4 days late costs 1.00.\n- `members.py`: the borrowing limit was 3, but the policy comment and tests say 5. I set `MAX_BORROWED = 5`.\n- `inventory.py`: `recent(n)` returned one event too many; it now returns the last `n`. I also made it return an empty list when `n <= 0`, which the tests didn't ask for.\n- `factory.py`: added the missing `Emma` book so the sample set has all three titles.\n- `books.py`: `parse_book` now turns the year into a number, so `age()` works.\n- `search.py`: it imported `normalize` from a module that doesn't exist (`catalog.nonexistent`); it now imports it from `catalog.text`.\n\nI didn't change any tests.INFO  2026-10-18T01:18:52 +0ms service=app name=lsp shutdown\nINFO  2026-10-18T01:18:52 +0ms service=app name=session shutdown\nINFO  2026-10-18T01:18:52 +0ms service=app name=mcp shutdown\n", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "param